{
  "chapter": "patterns/scale/sliding-window",
  "tier": "micro",
  "notes": [
    "A time-based window, not a count-based one. Events older than `windowMs` before",
    "`now` fall out; the boundary is inclusive, so an event exactly at the edge is still in.",
    "Times are plain integers and `now` is a parameter, so the edge is testable."
  ],
  "windowMs": 100,
  "cases": [
    {
      "id": "everything-inside-the-window-is-kept",
      "now": 100,
      "events": [
        { "id": "e1", "at": 50 },
        { "id": "e2", "at": 90 }
      ],
      "kept": ["e1", "e2"]
    },
    {
      "id": "an-event-older-than-the-window-falls-out",
      "now": 200,
      "events": [
        { "id": "old", "at": 50 },
        { "id": "new", "at": 150 }
      ],
      "kept": ["new"]
    },
    {
      "id": "the-edge-of-the-window-is-inclusive",
      "now": 200,
      "events": [{ "id": "edge", "at": 100 }],
      "kept": ["edge"]
    },
    {
      "id": "one-millisecond-past-the-edge-falls-out",
      "now": 200,
      "events": [{ "id": "just-out", "at": 99 }],
      "kept": []
    },
    {
      "id": "kept-events-hold-their-original-order",
      "now": 200,
      "events": [
        { "id": "a", "at": 120 },
        { "id": "b", "at": 110 },
        { "id": "c", "at": 190 }
      ],
      "kept": ["a", "b", "c"]
    },
    {
      "id": "an-event-in-the-future-is-kept",
      "now": 200,
      "events": [{ "id": "skewed", "at": 250 }],
      "kept": ["skewed"]
    },
    {
      "id": "everything-can-fall-out",
      "now": 1000,
      "events": [
        { "id": "a", "at": 10 },
        { "id": "b", "at": 20 }
      ],
      "kept": []
    },
    {
      "id": "an-empty-window-keeps-nothing",
      "now": 100,
      "events": [],
      "kept": []
    }
  ]
}
